{
  "v": 11,
  "label": "prefer-remote pulling over an item another source changed is settled by the collection's prefer-incoming",
  "note": "source a folded c3 into the item (its shared_object says so); b's server moved c1 to c2 at r2, the listing carrying it. b's placement holds c3 over its base c1, so the content axis meets both sides changed and b's prefer-remote pulls c2 (SYNC.md §5). The pull is then folded (§9): b changed (c2 against its base c1), the item changed for b (c3 against its shared_object c1) and the two disagree, a divergence the collection's prefer-incoming settles by adopting c2 and keeping c3, the body it replaced, as a retained item over b's handle, reported ContentChanged then Overruled. c3 is the body another source folded, not b's own edit: prefer-remote's keeping of a dropped local edit applies over an item that had not changed for the binding (§9), so c3 is kept once, by the collection's policy. b's base and shared_object move to c2; a's stay, so a owes c2 on its next sync",
  "store": {
    "collections": [{ "id": "Contacts", "account": null, "kind": "text/vcard", "conflict": "prefer-incoming" }],
    "objects": { "c1": { "body": "fixtures/card-basic.vcf" }, "c2": { "body": "fixtures/card-basic-edited.vcf" }, "c3": { "body": "fixtures/card-basic-renamed.vcf" } },
